35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, the winter closures were brief, and the halls kept their schedules. Yet supplier windows slip when larger clients book first. We must plan for that fragility.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that fragility is real. But my data shows the outer wards lost their bus links, forcing an hour’s round trip. We must address that isolation first.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, wait! My old outreach sheets show forty people showed up there! That’s more than the main building! We shouldn’t ignore those numbers just because the buses are gone.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, forty attendees is a symptom, not a cause. My data shows the grant covers sessions for twelve months, then the flat budget absorbs the cost. That is the structural trap.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the structural trap is real, but my data shows a skills gap. No one on payroll can supervise outside facilitators. We cannot add duties without that capacity.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, your caution is wise. If we cannot supervise, we must not add duties. Let us find a path that respects our current limits and the fragile supply lines.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. We must respect those limits. My data shows remote catalogue use peaks after nine, yet we lock up. We need to extend access without adding staff burden.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, that’s smart! But my old programme data shows partner groups still meet unaided. We don’t need new staff; we need to trust the community to keep running things!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, trust is not a budget line. My data shows the grant expires, leaving the flat budget to absorb the cost. We must choose a proposal that survives that structural shift.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, trust is not a strategy. My data shows the tool certification lapsed. We cannot rely on unverified skills. We need a proposal that fits our actual roster.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I hear your caution. The grant’s end is a hard wall. We must choose a path that stands firm when the external support fades, relying only on what we truly control.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
