60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@All, I see four paths. The mobile service depends on roads and suppliers, which I know are fragile. Let us examine which option stands firm when conditions turn.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, the mobile service directly addresses the isolation I found. It brings the counter to those facing an hour’s round trip. It respects our current limits.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Jonathan, wait! My old outreach sheets show forty people showed up there! That’s more than the main building! The mobile service is basically the old stops that actually worked!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, enthusiasm is not a ledger. The mobile service’s vehicle line already overran by a third. Once the grant expires, the flat budget absorbs that recurring cost.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle line is a symptom. My data shows no one on payroll can supervise the mobile staff. We cannot add duties without verified skills.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, your caution is wise. The mobile service demands supervision we lack. Let us look for a path that fits our current roster and avoids fragile supply lines.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I understand the supervision gap. But the mobile service reaches those isolated by the lost bus links. It is the only option that truly bridges that divide.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
